From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Subject: [PATCH] memories: write_words, the words a register file's write port
 writes
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

`write_words <address port> <word>...` in a regfile spec: the words that
write port writes, passed to generate_ram as -w_port_words. A word
written by one port then takes its data with no data mux. A port
without the line writes every word; a line naming no write port is
refused.

Carried in bazel-orfs, not upstreamed; needs OpenROAD's -w_port_words
(bazel-orfs patch 0159) and retires with the //:bump onto an ORFS and
OpenROAD that have them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Øyvind Harboe <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
---
 flow/scripts/memories/regfile_ram.py | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/flow/scripts/memories/regfile_ram.py b/flow/scripts/memories/regfile_ram.py
index 1eac6d18c..44a1e8679 100644
--- a/flow/scripts/memories/regfile_ram.py
+++ b/flow/scripts/memories/regfile_ram.py
@@ -48,6 +48,7 @@ KEYS = {
     "read",
     "read_banked",
     "write",
+    "write_words",
     "write_priority",
     "write_style",
     "zero_word",
@@ -163,6 +164,23 @@ def _args(lines: list[list[str]], block: str, shape: str) -> list[str]:
         # two ports writing one word in a cycle: OR their data by
         # default, as firtool's register files do
         args += ["-write_priority", _one(lines, "write_priority", "or")]
+    # `write_words <address port> <word>...`: the words a write port
+    # writes, the others it never addresses; a port without the line
+    # writes every word
+    reach = {line[0]: line[1:] for line in _values(lines, "write_words")}
+    if reach:
+        ports = [w[0] for w in _values(lines, "write")]
+        unknown = sorted(set(reach) - set(ports))
+        if unknown:
+            raise SystemExit(
+                f"regfile_ram: write_words names {', '.join(unknown)}, "
+                f"not a write port's address ({', '.join(ports)})"
+            )
+        every = [str(word) for word in range(words)]
+        args += [
+            "-w_port_words",
+            "{" + " ".join("{" + " ".join(reach.get(p, every)) + "}" for p in ports) + "}",
+        ]
     if int(_one(lines, "bank_columns", "1")) > 1 and not _values(
         lines, "bank_column_layout"
     ):
